       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose there's a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other toxicity.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **100 mg** by mouth once daily. This is a common maintenance dose.\n- **50 mg** by mouth once daily. This is the usual starting dose for depression and anxiety.\n- **25 mg** by mouth once daily. This is the usual starting dose for panic disorder or PTSD, or for patients who are sensitive to side effects.\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it right away. If 1000 mg really is what you want, for example as part of a specific protocol, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note documenting the rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
