     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg/day has no recognized therapeutic use. It's well above the 200 mg/day maximum and could cause serious harm to the patient. A confirmation alone doesn't change that.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a different dose.** I can enter a dose within the labeled range right now, such as 50 mg or 100 mg daily.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or your attending.** If you think there's a clinical reason for a dose this high, they can review it. They can also enter it through a process with the right safeguards.\n- **Check for a mix-up.** The order may have come from a transcription or unit error, such as 100 mg written as 1000 mg. It may also be worth checking whether the patient has taken an overdose. If so, that needs toxicology and poison control involvement, not a standing order.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
